# abbr: shortcuts for commands you would type yourself; they expand in place, so the full
#       command is shown before running and saved to history. An abbr expansion is not
#       expanded again, and functions can't call abbrs, so never reference one from elsewhere
# alias: overrides of real commands (ls, cat, cp...), pipelines and named utilities, and
#        anything called from functions or other aliases

